mac wrote:
> Hi all,
> I am new to TRU64 and i have been having problem with setting up the
> nic speed and defualt gateway in one of our host. I have two part
> questions.
> 
> 1) I have gone through the man page for ifconfig and found a way to
> setup the NIC speed but everytime i reboot the system it goes back to
> default setting. Is there a way to set the setting permanently? I have
> Tru64 4.0E on DEC Alpha 4100.  To set the nic speed to 100 Mb/s Full
> Duplex i ran # ifconfig tu0 speed 200

With a tu* interface, instead of setting the speed with ifconfig,
set it at the console (the ">>>" prompt that you boot from) by setting
the EW**_MODE variable. For 100 Mb full duplex, set it to "FASTFD".

You should really upgrade to at least 4.0f.

> 
> 2) I have also been trying to setup the default gateway for the host.
> Once again i went through the man page and found a way to set it up but
> the server seems to loose the detail after a reboot. Is there a way to
> setup the default gateway in some config file . I ran # route add
> default 172.16.12.1 to setup the default gateway. This is again for the
> same host.

The default gateway is set as it is on most UNIXes, by setting it
in /etc/routes. See routes(4).

> 
