sysconfig -q envmon gets you the current temp only.
If there was an environmental failure, it might have been logged in the
binary errorlog (type "man binlogd wsea ca uerf"), or it might still be
in the syslog daemon files (ls -l
var/cluster/members/{memb}/adm/syslog.dated/)

"/usr/sbin/sizer" will tell you some things about your system (-v
options tells you the OS version).  Once you know the OS version, you
can find more specific documentation about that version here:
http://h30097.www3.hp.com/docs/pub_page/doc_list.html
(the commands change every so often: 'hwmgr -view hier', a command that
addresses one of your questions, is only available after
V5-dot-<something>)

You want to look in the messages file for the "boot" occurance right
after the system went down (use the timestamps as a guide).  Is there a
"panic" right before that?

The HP page for your product is here:
http://h18002.www1.hp.com/alphaserver/archive/4100/?jumpid=oc_R1002_USENC-001_Compaq%20AlphaServer%204100&lang=en&cc=us



